  "description": "The annual working volume (AVOL) statistic: the total hours actually worked in the Swiss economy, plus its two per-job intensities. One cube carries three measures — the headline usual weekly hours per job (the \"Swiss work ~31h/week, not 42\" number), the annual hours worked per job, and the absolute annual volume of hours (~8.1 billion hours). All three cut by sex and by working-time category (full-time vs the two part-time bands), so the part-time gender split — Switzerland's defining labour-market feature — reads directly.",
